<title>SWEDEN: Nordbanken 9-mo profit rises 13 percent.</title>
<headline>Nordbanken 9-mo profit rises 13 percent.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial bank Nordbanken reports for nine months to September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profit			5,735   vs   5,091</p>
<p> Profit before credit losses	 6,224   vs   6,057</p>
<p> Interest income			20,796   vs  22,382</p>
<p> Interest costs			 12,966   vs  13,984</p>
<p> Interest net			    8,081   vs   8,673</p>
<p> Leasing income			    795   vs     814</p>
<p> Commission income		     1,889   vs   1,814</p>
<p> Commission costs			  314   vs     246</p>
<p> Net profit from financial trans.  1,027   vs     366</p>
<p> Other income				385   vs     582</p>
<p> Total income			   11,612   vs  11,728</p>
<p> Staff costs			     2,124   vs   2,057</p>
<p> Other costs			     2,456   vs   2,770</p>
<p> Depreciation				808   vs     844</p>
<p> Loan losses				 489   vs     966</p>
<p> Pension commitments		     130   vs     145</p>
<p> Tax charge				1,569   vs   1,271</p>
<p> Net profit				4,036   vs   3,675</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of state-controlled bank Nordbanken. Analysts polled by Reuters forecast a profit after credit losses of 5.49 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
